{{also|люди}}
==Serbo-Croatian==

===Etymology===
{{dercat|sh|ine-bsl-pro|ine-pro|inh=1}}
{{inh+|sh|sla-pro|*ľudьje}}, from {{inh|sh|ine-bsl-pro|*ljaudejes}}, nominative plural of {{m|ine-bsl-pro|*ljáudis}}, from {{inh|sh|ine-pro|*h₁léwdʰis}}.

===Noun===
{{sh-noun|g=m-p|head=љу̑ди}}; singular: {{l|sh|čȍvjek}} / {{l|sh|čȍvek}})

# [[people]], [[men]]
#: {{ux|sh|Два '''човјека''' су ишла цестом.|Two '''men''' walked down the street.}}
#: {{ux|sh|Пет '''људи''' је ишло цестом.|Five '''people''' walked down the street.}}
# {{lb|sh|colloquial}} [[guys]], [[you guys]] (group of familiar people of any or mixed gender)
# {{lb|sh|vocative}} [[everybody]], [[everyone]] (addressing a group of people)

====Usage notes====
This plural form takes suppletive stem in the singular, as can be seen in the declension table. Old dual forms have been preserved in the counting for 2, 3, 4 (also in 11, 12, 13, 14 etc.) which bind plural form of {{m|sh|чо̏вјек}} / {{m|sh|чо̏век}}.

